## What we learned, in compressed form

- **Toy environments teach the algorithm.** PPO on CartPole, LunarLander, Pendulum is not robotics — but it builds the intuition that everything in robot RL is built on.
- **Reading training source code beats reading documentation.** Every fix in Stage 2.5 came from reading `legged_robot.py`, not from docs. The training code is the ground truth.
- **Sim-to-sim transfer is real.** Even between simulators, physics differs. A policy must be re-tuned (or originally trained with enough randomization) to work across simulators.
- **Observation construction is part of the policy.** The 70-dim vector isn't just data; it's an interface, with strict ordering, scaling, and frame conventions. Get any of them wrong silently, and the robot fails.
- **Sustained walking on the first deployment is a real achievement.** Most beginners spend weeks here. You did it in days, because you debugged systematically and read source code.

